# React components (recap-engine)

## Folder template

```
ComponentName/
  ComponentName.tsx   # named function export only
  interface.ts        # Props (+ component-local types)
  styles.css          # only if the component owns styles
  index.ts            # re-exports component + Props
```

- Folder name = export name. Never nest `Recap/Recap/` beside `Recap/Recap.tsx`
- One canonical path per component — no parallel legacy + refactor copies
- Props with zero fields → skip `interface.ts`
- Export as `export function Stat(...)`, not `const Stat = (...)`

## Props

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
export type StatProps = {
  value: number
  classNames?: { root?: string; value?: string; unit?: string }
}

// Single root override
export type TitleProps = { className?: string; children: ReactNode }
```

- One root → `className?: string` + `cn('recap-x', className)`
- Multiple slots → `classNames?: { root?: string; ... }`
- Do not mix both APIs on one component without a clear reason
- Extend DOM types when wrapping native elements (`ButtonHTMLAttributes & { ... }`)

## Hooks

| Kind | Location |
|------|----------|
| Generic (`useSwipe`, `usePrefersReducedMotion`) | `src/hooks/` |
| Player/shell-only | `src/Recap/` next to consumer |
| Layout-only | `src/layouts/` |

- Return objects `{ ... }`, not long tuples
- Timers / rAF / listeners must clean up in `useEffect`
- Context hooks throw if used outside provider

## Context

- One session context; navigate with one naming scheme (`next`/`prev` or `goNext`/`goPrev`)
- Map to the other scheme once in an adapter (`useSceneCtx`), not ad hoc in every layout
